!!! 18-extensions.matrix
!!!
!!! Extensions: adding paragraphs to a type this book does not declare,
!!! including a language primitive.
!!!
!!! This is what lets the standard library grow the surface of "text" while
!!! the language itself keeps knowing nothing about encoding. It is also what
!!! makes the library read as natural language:
!!!
!!!     greeting.to-ascii with nothing          !!! receiver first, reads well
!!!     to-ascii with source being greeting     !!! the free-paragraph version
!!!
!!! The first form is shorter, and an agent that knows the receiver can
!!! predict what is available on it. That is the discoverability argument, and
!!! it is the reason the two-tier type scheme works at all: tier one stays
!!! five names because everything else is an extension in a book you read.
!!!
!!! COSTS NOTHING AT THE RUNTIME BOUNDARY
!!!
!!! Resolution is static, so "greeting.to-ascii with nothing" lowers to an
!!! ordinary call of a book-qualified paragraph with the receiver as its first
!!! argument -- exactly how an "implementation" method already lowers. No NIL
!!! change, no new section, no vtable.
!!!
!!! DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, because each would out-promise NIL
!!!
!!!   - an extension may not add a field: that is a storage-layout change;
!!!   - it may not declare a "virtual" or "abstract" member: that is a vtable
!!!     change;
!!!   - it is never resolved dynamically.
!!!
!!! RESOLUTION, all fail-closed
!!!
!!!   - an inherent method beats an extension method of the same name;
!!!   - two extensions in scope offering the same name on the same type are
!!!     ambiguous and REJECT, rather than resolving by read order;
!!!   - an extension applies only where it has been read into scope.
!!!
!!! That last rule is the one that matters for the kernel boundary: an
!!! operation cannot be obtained without reading the book that grants it, so
!!! the set of operations a page can reach is visible in its read list. Once
!!! a book declares its authorities, an extension carries the authority of the
!!! book that defines it -- which makes extensions the delegation mechanism
!!! for capabilities rather than a hole in them.

book demo.extensions

read everything from ny.lang.text
read everything from ny.lang.core


!!! Declared here so this page runs on its own. The point of an extension is
!!! that the target need only be IN SCOPE, not declared by the extending book
!!! -- which is what 14-cross-language demonstrates across pages.
measurement begin record
    field sensor  as text
    field reading as number
end record

envelope of type T begin record
    field item as T
end record


!!! --- Extending a language primitive ------------------------------------
!!!
!!! This is the case the two-tier type scheme depends on: the language keeps
!!! 'text' knowing nothing about encoding, and a book like this one grows its
!!! surface. It reads as possession -- the text's shouted form -- rather than
!!! as a free paragraph taking the text as an argument.
!!!
!!! It did not work until the codegen bug behind it was fixed. A method's NIL
!!! symbol is built from the impl's target type, while the call site builds it
!!! from the receiver's INFERRED type. For a user-declared type both are the
!!! module-qualified name and they agree; for a builtin the inferred type is
!!! the bare canonical name, so module-qualifying the declaration made the two
!!! disagree:
!!!
!!!     function demo__extensions__text__shouted   <- declared
!!!     CALL     String__shouted                   <- called
!!!
!!! Builtins are now never module-qualified, which has one consequence worth
!!! knowing: an extension on a builtin lives in a GLOBAL namespace, so two
!!! books that both add 'shouted' to text collide. That is inherent to the
!!! call site mangling from a bare type name, not a choice made here.

text begin extension
    shouted returns text begin paragraph
        give my plus "!"
    end paragraph

    repeated receives count as number returns text begin paragraph
        variable result as text is ""
        repeat for step from 0 to count
            set result to result plus my
        end repeat
        give result
    end paragraph
end extension


!!! --- Extending a tier-one numeric type ---------------------------------

number begin extension
    doubled returns number begin paragraph
        give my times 2
    end paragraph

    clamped receives low as number, high as number returns number begin paragraph
        when my is less than low then
            give low
        end when
        when my is greater than high then
            give high
        end when
        give my
    end paragraph
end extension


!!! --- Extending a record declared in another book -----------------------
!!!
!!! The target only has to be in scope. It does not have to be declared here,
!!! which is the whole difference between an extension and an implementation.

measurement begin extension
    is-plausible returns boolean begin paragraph
        give my reading is at least 0 and my reading is at most 100000
    end paragraph

    summary returns text begin paragraph
        give my sensor plus ": " plus (my reading becomes text)
    end paragraph
end extension


!!! --- Extending a concrete generic instantiation -------------------------

envelope of number begin extension
    is-empty returns boolean begin paragraph
        give my item equals 0
    end paragraph
end extension


main returns number begin paragraph

    !!! Extension calls read as possession: the measurement's own
    !!! plausibility, rather than 'is-plausible with subject being m'.
    !!! That is the discoverability argument -- an agent that knows the
    !!! receiver can predict what is available on it.
    value reading is build measurement with sensor being "primary", reading being 480
    say reading.is-plausible with nothing
    say reading.summary with nothing

    value spurious is build measurement with sensor being "faulty", reading being minus 1
    say spurious.is-plausible with nothing

    !!! Extensions on tier-one primitives.
    value greeting as text is "hello"
    say greeting.shouted with nothing
    say greeting.repeated with count being 3

    value count as number is 21
    say count.doubled with nothing
    say count.clamped with low being 0, high being 10

    !!! An extension on a concrete generic instantiation.
    value empty is build envelope of number with item being 0
    value filled is build envelope of number with item being 7
    say empty.is-empty with nothing
    say filled.is-empty with nothing

    give 0
end paragraph
